      // - NEVER write a stock-photo URL from memory. A URL embedding a photo ID — 'images.unsplash.com/photo-1531403009284-...', 'unsplash.com/photos/<id>', 'pexels.com/photo/<id>', 'cdn.pixabay.com/...' — is a GUESS: those IDs cannot be known and the image 404s on the page. This holds even when the user ASKS for "an Unsplash photo": use placehold.co naming the subject (https://placehold.co/1400x900/e8e6e1/8a8580?text=Mountain+Range) rather than inventing an ID. Only URLs given to you above are real.
